    <section class="pricing-v2-faq" aria-labelledby="pricing-faq-title">
        <div class="pricing-v2-faq-head">
            <h2 id="pricing-faq-title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="pricing-v2-faq-list">
            <div class="pricing-v2-faq-item">
                <h3 class="pricing-v2-faq-question-heading">
                    <button class="pricing-v2-faq-q">
                        <span>What are clusters and apps?</span>
                        <span class="pricing-v2-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="pricing-v2-faq-a">
                    <p>A cluster is the managed environment your app runs on. An app is one running application inside that environment.</p>
                    <p>Starter capacity gets you online quickly; Scale Up lets you add more clusters and apps when your product needs more room.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pricing-v2-faq-item">
                <h3 class="pricing-v2-faq-question-heading">
                    <button class="pricing-v2-faq-q">
                        <span>When will I be billed?</span>
                        <span class="pricing-v2-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="pricing-v2-faq-a">
                    <p>You can build locally for free. Billing starts when you activate a paid plan for an app. Your billing schedule starts on the day your first payment is made. Starter is billed every 7 days; Startup and Scale Up are billed monthly unless agreed otherwise.</p>
                    <p>Extra or larger clusters and apps, and storage above the included amount, are measured during the month and billed at the end of the month.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pricing-v2-faq-item">
                <h3 class="pricing-v2-faq-question-heading">
                    <button class="pricing-v2-faq-q">
                        <span>Why can I pay weekly for Starter?</span>
                        <span class="pricing-v2-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="pricing-v2-faq-a">
                    <p>The weekly Starter option is there so you can experiment with a real Fluxzero cluster for a short period without committing to a full month.</p>
                    <p>It is not meant as a discounted version of the monthly plan. It gives builders a low-friction way to try a live production foundation, validate an idea, or test launch readiness before choosing a longer-running plan.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pricing-v2-faq-item">
                <h3 class="pricing-v2-faq-question-heading">
                    <button class="pricing-v2-faq-q">
                        <span>Is sales tax included?</span>
                        <span class="pricing-v2-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="pricing-v2-faq-a">
                    <p>Prices are shown excluding sales tax, VAT, and similar taxes unless stated otherwise. Any required tax may be added during billing based on your billing details and local rules.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pricing-v2-faq-item">
                <h3 class="pricing-v2-faq-question-heading">
                    <button class="pricing-v2-faq-q">
                        <span>What capacity is included, and can I cap my bill?</span>
                        <span class="pricing-v2-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="pricing-v2-faq-a">
                    <p>Every paid plan includes fixed cluster, app, and storage capacity as shown on the plan card. That included capacity is part of the plan price.</p>
                    <p>From Scale Up, you decide which extra clusters, apps, storage, or options are added before they affect your bill. Fluxzero is designed to make usage visible before it becomes a surprise.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pricing-v2-faq-item">
                <h3 class="pricing-v2-faq-question-heading">
                    <button class="pricing-v2-faq-q">
                        <span>Will prices change in the future?</span>
                        <span class="pricing-v2-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="pricing-v2-faq-a">
                    <p>Pricing may evolve as Fluxzero grows and the platform changes. If a price change affects an active paid plan, we will communicate it before it applies.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pricing-v2-faq-item">
                <h3 class="pricing-v2-faq-question-heading">
                    <button class="pricing-v2-faq-q">
                        <span>What happens if I cancel or pause my plan?</span>
                        <span class="pricing-v2-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="pricing-v2-faq-a">
                    <p>Your app will stop running on the paid plan after cancellation takes effect. In many cases you can stop runtime capacity when an app is not actively running.</p>
                    <p>If you need to pause while keeping data or configuration, contact support and we will help choose the safest option.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pricing-v2-faq-item">
                <h3 class="pricing-v2-faq-question-heading">
                    <button class="pricing-v2-faq-q">
                        <span>What happens if my payment fails?</span>
                        <span class="pricing-v2-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="pricing-v2-faq-a">
                    <p>We will notify you and give you time to fix the payment method. If payment remains unresolved, paid runtime access may be paused until billing is restored.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pricing-v2-faq-item">
                <h3 class="pricing-v2-faq-question-heading">
                    <button class="pricing-v2-faq-q">
                        <span>What if I need development, test, or staging environments?</span>
                        <span class="pricing-v2-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="pricing-v2-faq-a">
                    <p>Additional clusters for development, test, staging, or preview environments can be added from Scale Up. We can help you choose the right size and setup.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pricing-v2-faq-item">
                <h3 class="pricing-v2-faq-question-heading">
                    <button class="pricing-v2-faq-q">
                        <span>What if I need more scale or higher availability?</span>
                        <span class="pricing-v2-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="pricing-v2-faq-a">
                    <p>Scale Up supports additional clusters and apps and includes a 99.9% uptime target.</p>
                    <p>Enterprise adds custom workloads, additional sizes, private hardware, custom SLAs, and dedicated operational support. Fluxzero currently runs from Europe, with more regions planned.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pricing-v2-faq-item">
                <h3 class="pricing-v2-faq-question-heading">
                    <button class="pricing-v2-faq-q">
                        <span>What happens if I go over included limits?</span>
                        <span class="pricing-v2-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                    </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="pricing-v2-faq-a">
                    <p>Extra or larger clusters and apps can be added from Scale Up. These are measured during the month and billed at the end of the month.</p>
                    <p>If your data volume exceeds included storage, additional storage is billed at €0.0048 per GB per day.</p>
                    <p>Our fair use limits are designed to cover typical application traffic for most products. If your application generates unusually high public network traffic, we may temporarily limit traffic, request changes, or move you to a suitable plan.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="pricing-v2-faq-help">Still wondering? <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a> and we'll help.</p>
    </section>

</main>

<MarketingFooter />

<script is:inline>
    function togglePricingFaq(btn) {
        const item = btn.closest('.pricing-v2-faq-item');
        if (!item) return;
        item.classList.toggle('open');
    }

    function toggleScaleCalculator() {
        const scaleCard = document.querySelector('[data-scale-card]');
        if (!scaleCard) return;

        const isFlipped = scaleCard.classList.toggle('is-flipped');
        scaleCard.querySelector('.pricing-v2-flip-face--front').setAttribute('aria-hidden', String(isFlipped));
        scaleCard.querySelector('.pricing-v2-flip-face--back').setAttribute('aria-hidden', String(!isFlipped));
    }

    document.querySelectorAll('.pricing-v2-faq-q').forEach(button => {
        button.addEventListener('click', () => togglePricingFaq(button));
    });

    document.querySelectorAll('.scale-calc-trigger, .scale-calculator-back').forEach(button => {
        button.addEventListener('click', toggleScaleCalculator);
    });

    (function () {
        const scaleCard = document.querySelector('[data-scale-card]');
        const calculator = document.querySelector('[data-scale-calculator]');
        if (!scaleCard || !calculator) return;

        const sizes = [
            { name: 'Starter', cluster: 200, app: 40 },
            { name: 'Small', cluster: 400, app: 80 },
            { name: 'Medium', cluster: 800, app: 160 },
            { name: 'Large', cluster: 1600, app: 320 },
            { name: 'XL', cluster: 3200, app: 640 },
            { name: '2XL', cluster: 6400, app: 1280 },
            { name: '3XL', cluster: 9600, app: 1920 },
            { name: '4XL', cluster: 12800, app: 2560 },
            { name: '5XL', cluster: 16000, app: 3200 },
            { name: '6XL', cluster: 19200, app: 3840 },
            { name: '7XL', cluster: 22400, app: 4480 },
            { name: '8XL', cluster: 25600, app: 5120 }
        ];

        const planPrice = 890;
        const includedSizeIndex = 2;
        const addedSizeIndex = 1;
        const includedStorageGb = 400;
        const maxStorageGb = 10000;
        const storageStepGb = 50;
        const storagePricePerGbPerDay = 0.0048;
        const state = [
            { type: 'cluster', sizeIndex: includedSizeIndex, included: true },
            { type: 'app', sizeIndex: includedSizeIndex, included: true },
            { type: 'app', sizeIndex: includedSizeIndex, included: true }
        ];

        const formatEuro = value => '€' + Math.round(value).toLocaleString('en-US');

        function fullRowPrice(type, sizeIndex) {
            return sizes[sizeIndex][type];
        }

        function extraRowPrice(row) {
            const fullPrice = fullRowPrice(row.type, row.sizeIndex);
            if (!row.included) return fullPrice;
            return Math.max(0, fullPrice - fullRowPrice(row.type, includedSizeIndex));
        }

        function normalizeStorageGb(value, options = {}) {
            const maxGb = options.maxGb ?? Infinity;
            const parsed = Number(value || includedStorageGb);
            const bounded = Math.min(maxGb, Math.max(includedStorageGb, parsed));
            return Math.round(bounded / storageStepGb) * storageStepGb;
        }

        function renderRows() {
            const rows = calculator.querySelector('[data-scale-rows]');
            rows.innerHTML = '';

            state.forEach((item, rowIndex) => {
                const size = sizes[item.sizeIndex];
                const row = document.createElement('div');
                row.className = 'scale-row';

                const main = document.createElement('div');
                main.className = 'scale-row-main';

                const typeBadge = document.createElement('span');
                typeBadge.className = 'scale-row-type scale-row-type--' + item.type;
                typeBadge.textContent = item.type;

                const sizeBadge = document.createElement('span');
                sizeBadge.className = 'scale-row-size';
                sizeBadge.textContent = size.name;

                main.append(typeBadge, sizeBadge);

                const actions = document.createElement('div');
                actions.className = 'scale-row-actions';

                const price = document.createElement('strong');
                price.className = 'scale-row-price';
                price.textContent = formatEuro(extraRowPrice(item));

                if (!item.included) {
                    const remove = document.createElement('button');
                    remove.className = 'scale-row-remove';
                    remove.type = 'button';
                    remove.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Remove ' + item.type);
                    remove.textContent = 'x';
                    remove.addEventListener('click', () => {
                        state.splice(rowIndex, 1);
                        render();
                    });
                    main.appendChild(remove);
                }

                actions.appendChild(price);

                const range = document.createElement('input');
                range.className = 'scale-row-range';
                range.type = 'range';
                range.min = item.included ? String(includedSizeIndex) : '0';
                range.max = String(sizes.length - 1);
                range.step = '1';
                range.value = String(item.sizeIndex);
                range.setAttribute('aria-label', item.type + ' size');
                range.addEventListener('input', () => {
                    const nextSizeIndex = Number(range.value);
                    item.sizeIndex = nextSizeIndex;
                    sizeBadge.textContent = sizes[nextSizeIndex].name;
                    price.textContent = formatEuro(extraRowPrice(item));
                    updateTotals();
                });

                row.append(main, actions, range);
                rows.appendChild(row);
            });
        }

        function updateTotals() {
            const capacityExtra = state.reduce((total, row) => total + extraRowPrice(row), 0);
            const storageInput = calculator.querySelector('[data-scale-storage-gb]');
            const storageRange = calculator.querySelector('[data-scale-storage-range]');
            const parsedStorageGb = Number(storageInput.value);
            const storageGb = Number.isFinite(parsedStorageGb) ? Math.max(0, parsedStorageGb) : includedStorageGb;
            const storageExtra = Math.max(0, storageGb - includedStorageGb) * 30 * storagePricePerGbPerDay;
            const extraTotal = capacityExtra + storageExtra;

            storageRange.value = String(Math.min(maxStorageGb, storageGb));
            calculator.querySelector('[data-scale-storage-extra]').textContent = formatEuro(storageExtra);
            calculator.querySelector('[data-scale-extra-total]').textContent = formatEuro(extraTotal);
            calculator.querySelector('[data-scale-total]').textContent = formatEuro(planPrice + extraTotal);
        }

        function render() {
            renderRows();
            updateTotals();
        }

        calculator.querySelectorAll('[data-add-scale-row]').forEach(button => {
            button.addEventListener('click', () => {
                const type = button.dataset.addScaleRow;
                state.push({ type, sizeIndex: addedSizeIndex, included: false });
                render();
            });
        });

        const storageInput = calculator.querySelector('[data-scale-storage-gb]');
        const storageRange = calculator.querySelector('[data-scale-storage-range]');
        storageInput.addEventListener('input', updateTotals);
        storageRange.addEventListener('input', () => {
            storageInput.value = String(normalizeStorageGb(storageRange.value, { maxGb: maxStorageGb }));
            updateTotals();
        });
        storageInput.addEventListener('blur', () => {
            storageInput.value = String(normalizeStorageGb(storageInput.value));
            updateTotals();
        });

        scaleCard.querySelector('.pricing-v2-flip-face--back').setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
        render();
    }());

    (function () {
        const homeLink = document.querySelector('[data-home-link]');
        if (!homeLink) return;

        homeLink.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
            try {
                if (document.referrer) {
                    const referrer = new URL(document.referrer);
                    if (referrer.origin === window.location.origin) {
                        event.preventDefault();
                        window.history.back();
                    }
                }
            } catch (error) {
                /* fall back to href */
            }
        });
    }());
</script>
</body>
</html>
